  "novel": "Barney [[revealed|reveal]] his dating [[philosophy|philosophy]]: the [[Platinum|platinum]] [[Rule|rule]]. \"[[Treat|treat]] women based on what you want,\" he [[explained|explain]].\n\nHis [[scheme|scheme]] was to date his doctor, but it [[spectacularly|spectacularly]] [[backfired|backfire]]. She [[ignored|ignore]] his calls and [[blocked|block]] his number. Barney was [[stunned|stun]].\n\n\"You [[broke|break]] your own rule,\" Ted [[observed|observe]]. \"You treated her the way you wanted, not the way she needed.\"\n\nBarney [[refused|refuse]] to [[admit|admit]] he was wrong. \"The rule is [[perfect|perfect]],\" he [[insisted|insist]]. \"The execution was off.\"\n\nBut deep down, Barney [[realized|realize]] the truth. The Platinum Rule, like all [[shortcuts|shortcut]] to love, was a trap. Real connections required honesty, not strategy.",
